"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole. The project has progressed through design and testing phases, with a development phase led by Omar Jensen starting next month. The team has expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions scheduled for September 10th. Budget allocations have been approved for training ($15,000) and compliance ($55,000). A significant milestone was reached with the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November. However, a recent email highlights critical budget and management roadblocks requiring immediate attention and confirmation."
